  +#13#10'"Json Pointer: Use / for levels, keys for objects, and numbers for in'
  +'dexes.\n"'#13#10'"Use * for all items, *#10 to join items by newline. Use ~'
  +' at the end of the path to return the raw JSON branch.\n"'#13#10'"Separate '
  +'multiple segments with semicolon ;.\n"'#13#10'"Literal: Text block in {'#226
  +#128#166'}. Special tag #10 for newlines. Use {{regex}} inside to extract da'
  +'ta directly into the text.\n"'#13#10'"Logic: If a Pointer in a segment is e'
  +'mpty, the whole segment is skipped. If a segment has no Pointer, only liter'
  +'al text blocks with embedded regular expressions are processed.\n"'#13#10'"'
  +'Regex: {prefix {regex[index]} suffix} inside a text block. If no [index] is'
  +' specified, the first match is used.\n"'#13#10'"Index can be a number, [*] '
  +'(join by space), or [*#10] (join by newline). If the regex finds no match, '
  +'the entire {'#226#128#166'} block is removed.\n"'#13#10'"Using ~ inside a r'
  +'egex returns the entire text.\n"'#13#10'"Inversion: Start a segment with ! '
  +'(e.g. !/path{Error}) to show its text only if the Pointer data is missing o'
  +'r the JSON is invalid.\n"'#13#10'"Commenting: /* text */ comments are strip'
  +'ped from the entire expression before any processing.\n"'#13#10'"Examples:\'
  +'n"'#13#10'"responseData/translatedText; matches/*#10/translation; /texts/te'
  +'xt; {literal text#10}; /result/text; /text{ ({(\\w+)})}; !/translations{Err'
