  +#155#180#230#148#185#229#144#151#239#188#159'"'#13#10#13#10'#: formconfig.rr'
  +'esponsehint'#13#10'msgid ""'#13#10'"Json Pointer: Use / for levels, keys fo'
  +'r objects, and numbers for indexes.\n"'#13#10'"Use * for all items, *#10 to'
  +' join items by newline. Use ~ at the end of the path to return the raw JSON'
  +' branch.\n"'#13#10'"Separate multiple segments with semicolon ;.\n"'#13#10
  +'"Literal: Text block in {'#226#128#166'}. Special tag #10 for newlines. Use'
  +' {{regex}} inside to extract data directly into the text.\n"'#13#10'"Logic:'
  +' If a Pointer in a segment is empty, the whole segment is skipped. If a seg'
  +'ment has no Pointer, only literal text blocks with embedded regular express'
  +'ions are processed.\n"'#13#10'"Regex: {prefix {regex[index]} suffix} inside'
  +' a text block. If no [index] is specified, the first match is used.\n"'#13
  +#10'"Index can be a number, [*] (join by space), or [*#10] (join by newline)'
  +'. If the regex finds no match, the entire {'#226#128#166'} block is removed'
  +'.\n"'#13#10'"Using ~ inside a regex returns the entire text.\n"'#13#10'"Inv'
  +'ersion: Start a segment with ! (e.g. !/path{Error}) to show its text only i'
  +'f the Pointer data is missing or the JSON is invalid.\n"'#13#10'"Commenting'
  +': /* text */ comments are stripped from the entire expression before any pr'
  +'ocessing.\n"'#13#10'"Examples:\n"'#13#10'"responseData/translatedText; matc'
  +'hes/*#10/translation; /texts/text; {literal text#10}; /result/text; /text{ '
  +'({(\\w+)})}; !/translations{Error: No data!#10}; /translations/0/text"'#13
